{"id":"G4797","lemma":"συγχέω","transliteration":"sugcheō","sayIt":"sugcheō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to confound","meaning":"συν-χέω\n(Rec. συγ-), [in LXX for בָּלַל, רָגַז, etc. ;]\nto pour together, commingle, confuse; metaphorically, confound, throw into confusion, stir up trouble: Act.21:27 (cf. συν-χύννω).†\n(AS)","glosses":["turmoil","bewilderment","confounded","stirred up"],"count":5,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"act-2","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"in bewilderment","kjv":"were confounded"}},{"chapterId":"act-9","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"he confounded","kjv":"confounded"}},{"chapterId":"act-19","v":32,"renderings":{"bsb":"in turmoil","kjv":"confused"}},{"chapterId":"act-21","v":27,"renderings":{"bsb":"They stirred up","kjv":"stirred up"}},{"chapterId":"act-21","v":31,"renderings":{"bsb":"was in turmoil"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Acts 2:6","note":"When this sound was heard, the multitude came together and were bewildered, because everyone heard them speaking in his own language.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G4862","lemma":"σύν","transliteration":"sun","gloss":"with"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}